course: dictionary
lesson: 10293
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. «A toucan picks fruit with the tip of its beak» is about a bird. «The children waited at the toucan crossing» is about a road.
explain: A dictionary often numbers the meanings, like 1) and 2), and marks where a meaning is used, like (UK). Look for clues such as fruit, forest or branch for the bird, and road, cross or cyclists for the crossing.
explain: Toucan is a noun, so it names a thing: one toucan, or several toucans. Before you decide what a word means, read every numbered meaning and test each one in the sentence.
fact: A toucan is a tropical bird from Central and South America, with black feathers and a huge, brightly coloured beak.
fact: «A toucan's huge beak is light because it is a honeycomb of bone covered with keratin.» Inside, it is hollow, full of air spaces.
fact: The beak helps a toucan reach fruit on thin branches, and it lets the bird lose heat to keep cool.
fact: Toucans spread seeds through the forest.
fact: In the UK, a toucan crossing is a road crossing with lights that both pedestrians and cyclists can use. Say it as «two can» cross.
exercise: «A toucan picks fruit with the tip of its beak and flicks it back into its throat.» What is a toucan in this sentence? | A type of fruit | *A tropical bird with a huge beak | A tall tree in the forest | A road crossing with lights
exercise: In UK road safety lessons, what is a toucan crossing for? | *A place where pedestrians and cyclists can cross together | A place to pick fruit | A safe spot for birds to build nests | A place where only cars can drive
exercise: «Parrots and toucans have two toes pointing forward and two pointing back.» How many toes does a toucan have pointing forward? | Three | Four | One | *Two
test: «The toucan's beak is light because it is hollow inside.» Why is the beak light? | It is made of metal | It is full of water | *It is full of air spaces, like a honeycomb | It is painted black
test: Which sentence uses toucan to mean a road crossing? | *The toucan crossing let the cyclists and walkers cross together | The toucan tossed a grape up and caught it | The toucan spread seeds through the forest | The toucan hovered near the fruit
exam: Why does a toucan's beak help the bird? | It is used to dig holes in the ground | It helps the bird swim fast under water | It helps the bird fight off other birds | *It helps the bird reach fruit on thin branches and lose heat to keep cool
